      "content": "The mass number depends on the number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus, which do not change during chemical ionisation. Let's look at the electron configuration instead. If an atom in Group 1 has an electron configuration ending in $s^1$, what happens to that outer electron when it forms an $X^+$ ion?"
